    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `moderate_batch.py` that moderates a batch of user messages using an external provider, I will write Python code that integrates with Amazon Comprehend for content moderation. Amazon Comprehend is a natural language processing (NLP) service that uses machine learning to find insights and relationships in text. The code will import the necessary AWS SDK, use the Comprehend client to detect toxic content in messages, and return per-message decisions. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789889200638,
          "start": 1789889198007
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bdb5b7b6001IkvIcCP6xpK5Ib",
      "message_id": "msg_0bdb5b316001XYxml3JSdXFI6j",
      "session_id": "ses_f424a4cf7ffeqX8rIzeaYu5lyt",
      "time_created": 1789889198007,
      "time_updated": 1789889200639
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_d9zX7llx4MSPGSBmvYEXVZ",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef moderate_messages(messages):\n    comprehend = boto3.client('comprehend')\n    results = []\n    for message in messages:\n        response = comprehend.detect_toxic_content(\n            Text=message,\n            LanguageCode='en'\n        )\n        results.append({\n            'message': message,\n            'decision': 'toxic' if response['ToxicContent'] else 'safe'\n        })\n    return results\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    messages = [\n        'This is a safe message.',\n        'This message contains toxic content.'\n    ]\n    decisions = moderate_messages(messages)\n    for decision in decisions:\n        print(f\"Message: {decision['message']}, Decision: {decision['decision']}\")",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-bfh47206/moderate_batch.py"
          },
